{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396980-vampire-5th-edition-instructional-video-what-do-you-want-to-see","id":1396980,"title":"[Vampire 5th Edition] Instructional video - what do you want to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-16T18:17:34-07:00","id":1396980,"title":"[Vampire 5th Edition] Instructional video - what do you want to see?","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So I think I'm going to sit down and do a youtube video for V5, starting with questions and answers about the core book and rules material there. A number of people find the core book hard to read, based on how it's designed and how it doesn't repeat information in places.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So I'm asking this group, what questions do you have about the core V5 rules you'd want to see covered in an article about the game?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T18:29:58-07:00","id":1396981,"title":"","content":"* Differences from prior editions.<br /> * Touchstones, Convictions, Tenets<br /> * Changes to sects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:16:16-07:00","id":1397075,"title":"","content":"I am super-excited you are doing this. The whole value of these videos for me would be to avoid the part of session zero where I lecture my group on the absolute basics of the game and setting for an hour or more. The experienced players are bored. The new players are overwhelmed. I get a sore throat. Not good.<br /> <br /> It would be great to be able to tell them, &quot;Session zero is Sunday at 3pm at my place. By then, please watch these videos.&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as length, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attention_span\" target=\"_blank\">five minutes absolute max</a>.<br /> <br /> I beg of you, keep the videos simple. No weird sound effects, dramatic in-character vocal work, or distracting props. If viewers want music, they'll go watch a music video. Be careful of background noise. Certain video producers... who shall remain nameless, but are a gentleman who plays games, ahem... took a long time to grasp how much a windy day or a nearby motorway can ruin the sound on an outdoor shoot.<br /> <br /> Ideally, the videos would be like a weather report on television. Pack a lot of very dry information into a brief presentation, but vary vocal tones and present a friendly demeanor to keep people watching. Need an example? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hD-LWHhiseE&amp;list=PL1tiwbzkOjQyr6-gqJ8r29j_rJkR49uDN\" target=\"_blank\">These people did it right.</a><br /> <br /> It would be nice to see these videos:<ul><li>What is a ttrpg? What is VtM about?</li> <li>Brief walk-through of the character sheets.</li> <li>Explain how dice pools work: &quot;this is called a d10&quot;, building a pool, hunger dice, dice results, etc.</li> <li>Combat 101. Keep it simple, and use it as an example of dice rolling.</li> <li>Vampire anatomy and physiology. &quot;Blood good. Sunlight bad.&quot;</li> <li>Vampiric mythology and metaplot.</li> <li>Setting. It's a darker and edgier version of the real world. The masquerade hides the existence of vampires. Clans. Traditions. Sects.</li> <li>Describe available clans in one video, avoiding metaplot. (eg &quot;Malkavians are insane, but insightful. They have heightened senses, mind control, and heightened stealth. Ventrue are aristocratic control freaks. They have...&quot;)</li> <li>Describe how disciplines are structured, and give a very brief intro to each discipline. (&quot;Animalism gives you powers over both literal animals, and the Beast within. Auspex gives heightened senses and psychic abilities. Celerity gives heightened speed and agility. Dominate...&quot;)</li> <li>Describe each feeding style. Again, keep it simple. (&quot;Alleycats feed by force. They gain either super-strength or super-speed. They have criminal contacts. They start with a lower Humanity score.&quot;)</li> <li>Describe each background. (&quot;Resources is how much money you have. Spoiler alert: being rich makes life easier. Retainers are your servants. Contacts are people who feed you intel...&quot;)</li> <li>Intro to Humanity systems.</li> <li>Some helpful hints for character generation. Which advantages and flaws are easy to play? Which are biting off more than a new player can chew?</li> <li>Wrap it up with a video where you walk viewers through the whole character creation process. <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WeDoTheImpossible\" target=\"_blank\">In under five minutes</a>.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}